4549d5ca19c7ebf6835ea33d67b59d47c961d6a7ab728c7e781bb5bc83c93f3e  partial-RM_ROT-marker
# M6.5 (2026-06-21): LUT-KCM RM = 4x4 baked-weight TPU + VPU. The 16 INT8 weights
# are editable LUT-INIT (8 dont_touch LUT6/PE, INIT[0]=weight bit -> "the logic is
# the model"). This static ALSO carries AXI HWICAP @0x41400000 so a weight bit can
# be ICAP-edited live (M6.5.2). impl_7 placed: RP RM 3559/4400 LUT (81%), static
# 3649 (incl HWICAP), DSP 20->4, DRC 0, pr_verify impl_1-vs-impl_7 compatible.
# A live ICAP weight edit yields a partial NOT on this list -> M5 gate refuses it,
# exactly as intended (edited != trusted-as-built).
56372522387f6e427b861caa57f9b26b9ed6b53f1c2621c7a077ad951f4d16bf  full-static+RM_LUTKCM-hwicap
b033284535b0c14fdf900926151fdebbe869b8a39d9a61e43db55ebca3ef8065  partial-RM_LUTKCM-baked
# M7.0b (2026-06-21): on-chip XOR TRAINING firmware baked into the NEORV32 IMEM.
# Same DFX static structure as M6.3 (rm_tpuvpu RM, VPU bypassed — training reads
# the raw INT32 RES0-3 and does backprop/SGD in SW); only the IMEM image differs,
# so the full-static hash is new. Boot this full static, watch the LOSS curve fall
# over UART (host does no math). Built from vivado/dfx build impl_5.
